{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00175",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.9,
      "end_seconds": 4.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Okay, welcome. Let's see what's going on. What's been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.89,
      "end_seconds": 13.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.13,
      "text": "Well, um, I've been having burning when I pass urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.63,
      "end_seconds": 15.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "And when did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 17.68,
      "end_seconds": 24.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.03,
      "text": "Hmm, it's been going on for about two weeks. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.11,
      "end_seconds": 34.19,
      "duration_seconds": 9.08,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps. Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.11,
      "end_seconds": 55.76,
      "duration_seconds": 20.65,
      "text": "It comes and goes. It's severe, honestly. I've had an urgent need to pass urine too, for three days. I've also been needing to go all the time, for ten days. With needing to go all the time, mild, I'd say. There was pain low in the tummy, yes, but that went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.96,
      "end_seconds": 59.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Did you manage to eat before coming?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.06,
      "end_seconds": 63.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Yes, I had something small this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.92,
      "end_seconds": 70.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.88,
      "text": "Any vaginal discharge, blood in the urine, vomiting or back pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.41,
      "end_seconds": 77.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "No vaginal discharge, blood in the urine, vomiting or back pain, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.11,
      "end_seconds": 80.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.35,
      "end_seconds": 85.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "No, um, nothing with my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.55,
      "end_seconds": 88.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 91.44,
      "end_seconds": 93.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "It's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.02,
      "end_seconds": 96.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.0,
      "end_seconds": 106.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "It's pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast for my acidity. I'd been on metformin, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.89,
      "end_seconds": 111.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.42,
      "end_seconds": 124.05,
      "duration_seconds": 11.63,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.36,
      "end_seconds": 125.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 126.4,
      "end_seconds": 128.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "No, never had any surgery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.25,
      "end_seconds": 134.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "Have you been able to keep up with your usual activities?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.14,
      "end_seconds": 147.69,
      "duration_seconds": 12.55,
      "text": "Oh, you know, for the most part, yes. I just carry on and try not to dwell on things too much, though I won't pretend it hasn't crossed my mind a few times."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.17,
      "end_seconds": 153.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.02,
      "end_seconds": 156.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.19,
      "end_seconds": 159.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.31,
      "end_seconds": 161.06,
      "duration_seconds": 0.75,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.42,
      "end_seconds": 173.74,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.62,
      "end_seconds": 180.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "I've got diabetes. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.12,
      "end_seconds": 182.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "Okay, I'm following."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.35,
      "end_seconds": 189.48,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "I, I have acid reflux. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.96,
      "end_seconds": 195.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.8,
      "end_seconds": 196.58,
      "duration_seconds": 0.78,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.54,
      "end_seconds": 215.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.74,
      "end_seconds": 225.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "Just relax your arm..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.27,
      "end_seconds": 245.75,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 97 percent on room air, blood pressure 118 over 82, pulse 73. And temperature is 36.7 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.3,
      "end_seconds": 247.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.16,
      "end_seconds": 251.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "We'll put it in context in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.04,
      "end_seconds": 255.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.19,
      "end_seconds": 256.96,
      "duration_seconds": 0.77,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.75,
      "end_seconds": 269.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Okay, here we go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.15,
      "end_seconds": 274.68,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.66,
      "end_seconds": 276.36,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.39,
      "end_seconds": 279.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.76,
      "text": "Bear with me a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.67,
      "end_seconds": 300.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "There's mild tenderness above the pubic bone, and no tenderness in the loins."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.58,
      "end_seconds": 316.83,
      "duration_seconds": 10.25,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.89,
      "end_seconds": 321.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 322.0,
      "end_seconds": 322.9,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.28,
      "end_seconds": 346.31,
      "duration_seconds": 17.03,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Right, here's what I'm thinking. I think we're dealing with a urinary tract infection at this stage. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. It could also be a kidney infection, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.74,
      "end_seconds": 349.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.05,
      "end_seconds": 366.03,
      "duration_seconds": 15.98,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a urinary tract infection is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had burning when you pass urine for about two weeks, severe, and no vomiting or vaginal discharge."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 367.02,
      "end_seconds": 370.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Um, you know, yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.34,
      "end_seconds": 388.39,
      "duration_seconds": 16.05,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 388.69,
      "end_seconds": 390.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.23,
      "end_seconds": 394.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "We should do a urine culture for urinary symptoms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 395.67,
      "end_seconds": 399.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "I can book that for Tuesday at 3:30 pm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 402.49,
      "end_seconds": 412.44,
      "duration_seconds": 9.95,
      "text": "We should do a urine test for urinary symptoms. I'm prescribing trimethoprim, 200 milligrams, twice a day, for three days. That should help with urine infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.9,
      "end_seconds": 414.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 415.66,
      "end_seconds": 434.99,
      "duration_seconds": 19.33,
      "text": "Drink plenty of water and don't hold it in when you need to go. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. Keep an eye out, and if you get a fever, back pain or vomiting, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 435.56,
      "end_seconds": 438.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Oh, uh, yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 442.72,
      "end_seconds": 453.03,
      "duration_seconds": 10.31,
      "text": "Please come and see me if it's not better in three days. I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 453.83,
      "end_seconds": 464.28,
      "duration_seconds": 10.45,
      "text": "So, I take the trimethoprim, 200 milligrams, twice a day and come back if it's not better in three days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 465.2,
      "end_seconds": 469.38,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Alright, that's everything from me. Any other questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 473.4,
      "end_seconds": 476.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "No, you've explained it well. Thanks."
    }
  ]
}